    "created_at": "2016-06-24T18:20:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-24T18:20:32Z",
    "body": "Sorry for not replying before. I think this entrypoint was redundant. It was originally added for feature and fallback detection, for web pages that wanted e.g. both WebGL and 2D Canvas code paths. The fact is though that these web pages can try creating a WebGL context, and if that doesn't work, fall back to creating a 2D context. This technique has been used by many web pages to date and seems to be working fine; the cost of (failed) context creation isn't that high, and the only way to _really_ know whether you'll get a context of a certain type is to try creating it, not to ask whether it's \"probably\" supported.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
